{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1439340-changeling-penal-units-they-can-be-a-great-plot-device","id":1439340,"title":"Changeling penal units, they can be a great plot device","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-11T18:57:51-08:00","id":1439340,"title":"Changeling penal units, they can be a great plot device","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Im not saying anything original or that the game disagrees with that. It's just the conclusion I've come to in my game. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In my game a brief rebellion occurred. And the players managed to defeat the enemy leader (A duke of house gwydion) before the big battle, the rest of his forces tried to retaliate but lost their will after seeing the king\u2019s forces. The Duke nephew, a countess surrendered the remaining forces in exchange for mercy. The king agreed to and the enemy forces has to take a geas in which the sworn to never take arms against concordia during this life, and that they would have to repay the treason with their aid. They basically became a penal unit. They were not used during the war, because some shenanigans could always happen to make them aid rebels somehow. But they appeared in the chronicle later as a task force against powerful chimeras. If they survived the battle they would earn their freedom back.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This happend naturally in my table. So I thought maybe entire penal units of changelings should be more common. Even in times of peace, changelings who have to obey a geas because of terrible crimes can probably be grouped together and work as a single unit. This opens up several plot hooks.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-What if there is a sidhe who schemes to incriminate changelings and add more servants to the penal colony? This could be a whole metaphor for the USA penal system and different from reality it could end with a sweet sweet ending where the sidhe ends up in kingdom the penal unit.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-The penal unit comes to town, and then some crimes begin to happen, the motley is tasked to investigate. Will they give in to the easy answer of thinking it\u2019s the penal unit or discover who the true criminal is? Again, a good way to discuss real life subjects in the game.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-The entire motley is unfairly (or fairly depending on the PC actions) incriminated and now you can have a whole chronicle about the challenges they have to face until they earn their freedom back, or how they can escape this situation before. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-The nobles decide to give the PCs a boon, they will be tasked with a fraction of the penal unit, and they can order whatever they want (within reason) to it. What will they do with this sudden (but possibly) problematic help? Will they earn favours by bossing this smaller unit around? Use it to the benefit of their community? Earn the penal unit gratitude by letting they get off easy? </span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Anyway. Penal units seem like an interesting tool to use on a CTD game. And contrary to the real world, it can work even better when sovereign, oaths and geas are into play. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 03-11-2021, 10:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T22:51:03-08:00","id":1439383,"title":"","content":"I like it, and Sovereign and Contract would make this a thing so easily. I love me some Dead Legion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T02:54:52-08:00","id":1439407,"title":"","content":"Great idea, I'm stealing this straight away!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}